# The join from the roles of the frames to the roles of the acts of k.actions: in a frame of `act`, the role `role`
# is the k.actions role `act_role`; `marker=yes` when it captures the preposition that marks that role (the rel of
# "at table 1" marks the place). A map with `frame` holds for that frame only; one with `takes` for the parts that
# take that (a rel that takes a preposition marks the place, one that takes a direction word is the direction).
# A role of a frame with no map is the k.actions role of the same name.
@w.lang.en.role_map core.type of=w.lang.en.role_map shared=true closed=true core.source="hand-core 1"
